"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Bank of America and Goldman Sachs disclose that their preferred single point of entry resolution strategy, whether under the U.S. Bankruptcy Code or the FDIC's Orderly Liquidation Authority (OLA), results in significant or complete losses for parent company security holders while protecting third-party creditors of subsidiaries. BAC states that security holders could face 'significant or complete losses' while third-party creditors of subsidiaries receive recoveries (bac_2024_1A_P033_S001). Similarly, GS notes that losses at the subsidiary level would be transferred to Group Inc. and borne by security holders, resulting in 'significant and possibly complete losses' for Group Inc.'s security holders, while third-party creditors of subsidiaries receive full recoveries (gs_2024_1A_P147_S001, gs_2024_1A_P147_S002). GS further details that OLA allows the FDIC to disregard strict priority of creditor claims, a specific mechanism also implied in BAC's discussion of OLA outcomes.",
