"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and JPMorgan Chase explain that their single-point-of-entry resolution strategies subject parent equity holders and unsecured creditors to losses first. BAC discloses that its 'single point of entry' strategy may result in security holders suffering greater losses than under bankruptcy, with parent equity held solely for creditors (bac_2024_1A_P032_S002, bac_2024_1A_P032_S003). JPMorgan confirms that under its resolution strategy, losses are imposed first on holders of the Parent Company's equity securities and thereafter on unsecured creditors, including eligible long-term debt (jpm_2024_1A_P038_S001, jpm_2024_1A_P039_S002). Both firms highlight that this structure prioritizes the continuity of operating subsidiaries at the expense of the parent's investors.",
