"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Morgan Stanley aligns with Bank of America on the risks of the FDIC's Orderly Liquidation Authority (OLA) and Single Point of Entry (SPOE) strategy. BAC warns that OLA and SPOE may result in security holder losses (bac_2024_1A_P032_S003, bac_2024_1A_P033_S001). MS similarly states that the FDIC may apply OLA powers, which include the power to 'disregard the priority of creditor claims,' adversely impacting unsecured debt holders, and identifies the SPOE strategy as the 'reasonably likely outcome' if OLA is applied to a G-SIB (ms_2024_1A_P062_S002, ms_2024_1A_P063_S001). Both highlight the specific risk that OLA powers differ from standard bankruptcy priority protections.",
